{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler who reigned over the County of Tripoli from 1183 to 1187. He was a significant figure in the Crusades and a key player in the political landscape of the Levant during the 12th century. His reign marked a period of both prosperity and conflict for the County.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond III was the son of Raymond IV Count of Tripoli. He inherited the county upon his father's death in 1183. His early reign was characterized by consolidating his power and rebuilding the county after a period of instability. He strengthened the county's defenses and fostered economic growth. He faced challenges from neighboring powers including the Seljuk Turks and the Ayyubid dynasty. He skillfully navigated these threats maintaining Tripoli's independence.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Crusades*\n\nRaymond III played a prominent role in the Third Crusade. He participated in the siege of Acre a crucial port city in the Levant. He also fought against the Ayyubid forces in Syria. His military campaigns demonstrated his strategic acumen and his commitment to defending the Christian territories in the region. He established alliances with other Crusader states and played a vital role in bolstering the Crusader presence in the Levant. His military successes enhanced Tripoli's prestige and solidified its position as a significant power within the Crusader sphere.\n\n*Political and Economic Policies*\n\nRaymond III implemented policies aimed at strengthening Tripoli's economy and political stability. He fostered trade and agriculture promoting economic prosperity within the county. He also worked to maintain a balance of power among the various factions within Tripoli’s society. His reign saw improvements in infrastructure and the development of a more robust administrative system. He prioritized maintaining relations with both Christian and Muslim communities demonstrating a pragmatic approach to governance. His policies contributed to the long-term stability and prosperity of the County of Tripoli.\n\nRaymond III's reign was a pivotal period in the history of the County of Tripoli. His leadership during the Crusades and his efforts to stabilize the county's economy and politics left a lasting legacy. He is remembered as a skilled military leader a shrewd politician and a capable administrator. His reign represents a significant chapter in the history of the Crusader states and the Levant. He successfully defended Tripoli's independence and fostered a period of relative peace and prosperity.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1805190145969391}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.8874615458771586e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.07509470731019974}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.02148974873125553}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5968805551528931}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5940437912940979}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.5694845914840698}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5716680884361267}, {"token": "▁over", "logprob": -1.4142320156097412}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00020037073409184813}, {"token": "▁County", "logprob": -0.05721329525113106}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -1.5139465176616795e-05}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.013013552874326706}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0033693707082420588}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.000163541772053577}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0006127863889560103}, {"token": "8", "logprob": -1.8529095649719238}, {"token": "3", "logprob": -0.1145518571138382}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.17996035516262054}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0008241117466241121}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -2.0265558760002023e